The export is a snapshot from 4 October 2026, not the live support queue. The old incident page says one issue and one fix; its computed views contradict that summary. Keep the shared parser fault and the booking-v3 hint fault in separate tickets.

## Engineering outcome · 5 October 2026

The course desk update says #4471 closed on 5 October. The parser outcome is **FIXED**: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The hint outcome is **WON’T FIX** because booking-v3 was retired. These are different resolutions: retirement is not evidence that the hint was repaired. The GitHub parser ticket is closed as completed; the hint ticket is closed as not planned. The five unusual reports remain observations within the parser classification, not a third confirmed cause or five additional reports. The update does not establish a separate fix for those symptoms.

Source: [course engineering update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows#engineering-update), checked 1 November 2026. The data below remains the 4 October export, so later activity is not present in its charts.

