## Separate fixes

- **Shared parser:** day-first tenants have app, email, and booking-v2 dates read month first. For example R-41200 intended 7 April but received 4 July. Parse using an explicit agreed date format or structured date input; test day-first tenants across all channels. The code's parser count includes the residual reports below.
- **booking-v3 hint:** for day-first tenants, the form prints MM/DD/YYYY while interpreting input in the tenant's order. Copper Studio, Alder Physio and Pale Harbour use this form. Align the hint and form interpretation; test the same tenant through form and app because they can have different causes. Intake browser locale and intakeTag are not reliable classifiers.
- **Unresolved one-day/timing symptoms:** investigate the desk-note report IDs separately, preserving their current classification and avoiding double counting. Compare original timestamps, local dates, timezone offsets, date-only conversions and reminder scheduling. Do not assert a timezone root cause from these reports alone. Recheck whether R-41236's early invite belongs with a date shift or is another timing fault.

## Reports continue while the desk merges

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The received series and the merged series answer different questions. Backlog processing can create a merge spike. The export has no proof that the queued fix has shipped. The later engineering update above supplies the closure outcomes; it does not change these historical counts.

## Replace subject-only deduplication

The accepted 2024 decision and its triage page are stale under the kb's 180-day rule. Matching subject lines is not evidence of a shared cause. Keep the accepted decision unchanged; propose decision 0002 to supersede it after desk approval.

<DedupeExplorer />

Read the body, identify tenant locale and booking form, and compare channel and reproduction before merging. Same tenant and different channels can mean different faults; different subjects can describe the same fault. Unknown tenants require investigation rather than automatic merging. Keep report IDs and counts traceable, and review continuing arrivals after any fix.

See [proposed decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause).

